ame="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1170324A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>DAINIPPON INK &amp; CHEMICALS</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MOTOMIYA SHIGERU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NONAKA SHINICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DAINIPPON INK AND CHEMICALS, INC.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MOTOMIYA, SHIGERU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NONAKA, SHINICHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MOTOMIYA SHIGERU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NONAKA SHINICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MOTOMIYA, SHIGERU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NONAKA, SHINICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A sheet-form photocurable material which comprises (a) a polymerizable unsaturated monomer, (b) a polymer which is either polymethyl methacrylate or a high-molecular polymer consisting mainly of methyl methacrylate units and which is compatible with or swollen with the monomer (a), (c) a photocuring agent, and (d) a fibrous reinforcement.  It is excellent in productivity, handleability, and photocurability.  The material is usable for producing a layered molding and forming a backup layer (reinforcing layer) of a molded article.  It is useful as a retreading protective material for pipes, covering material, lining material, fixing material, etc.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une matière photodurcissable en forme de feuille comprenant: (a) un monomère insaturé polymérisable; (b) un polymère qui est soit un méthacrylate de polyméthyle soit un polymère à poids moléculaire élevé formé principalement d'unités de méthacrylate de méthyle et qui est compatible ou gonflé avec le monomère (a); (c) un agent photodurcissant; et (d) un renfort fibreux. La matière selon l'invention possède d'excellentes propriétés de productivité, de maniabilité et une excellente aptitude au durcissement induit par la lumière. On peut utiliser cette matière pour produire une moulage en couches et pour former une couche de support (couche de renfort) d'un article moulé. Elle s'utilise comme matière protectrice de rechapage de tuyaux, comme matière de recouvrement, de doublure, de fixation, etc.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>